    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46567" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ηη</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦτα</span></b>  (q.v.), τό,
		indecl., eighth (later seventh) letter of the Gr.
		alphabet; as numeral <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκτώ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄγδοος</span>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνυμ̓</span>,= <i><span class="en">
			8
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			000
		</span></i>. In most local alphabets of <span class="entity">v B.C.</span> and earlier it
		represents <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>h</i>, in others
			(incl. the 
				Ion.
			= later general Gr. alphabet) one of the long
				<i>ē</i> sounds (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῆ
			βῆ</span>). Described by <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				382.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Agatho
				4.2
			</span></i>.</div>
